LAW|n=ERRATA (method law)|name=Amend in place, preserve the superseded wording here and nowhere else|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=wrong-errata-liris|statement=Interior: "Each entry states what the law said, what was measured, what the text now says, and why. The law body is amended in place so it does not contradict itself; the superseded wording is preserved here and nowhere else." And: "an unconditional sentence with a contradicting footnote is a law that argues with itself. The generalisation was the error, not the measurement, so the sentence now carries its scope." A machine must repair an over-generalised law by rewriting the sentence to carry its scope — not by ap|json=0
LAW|n=ERRATA-1|name=Sectioned key pays — the measured reversal|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=wrong-errata-liris|statement=Interior, measured 2026-07-27 (measurements/play_hutter.py, receipt FABLE5-KEY-PAYS-SECTIONED.hbp), order-2 adaptive model + 32-bit range coder, key warmed symmetrically and never in the stream, 12 x 100,000 B: baseline payload 524,051, total 524,051, bpc 3.4937; KEY prior3174 payload 516,880, +charge 3,174, total 520,054, bpc 3.4670, net -3,997 WINS; MYTHOS key payload 517,547, +charge 3,174, total 520,721, bpc 3.4715, net -3,330 WINS. Per-section saving 598 / 542 B. Break-even 5.31 sections. 36/36 round-trips byt|json=0
LAW|n=ERRATA-1 (limit clause)|name=Sectioning does not launder noise|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=wrong-errata-liris|statement=Interior: "the RANDOM arm still hurts before charging (-102 B). A good prior amortises; noise does not become good by being sectioned." A machine must test a candidate prior against a random arm before amortising it across sections; a negative pre-charge saving disqualifies the prior regardless of section count.|json=0
LAW|n=Function Law 1 (VIII.C)|name=The Idempotent Dedup Law|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=second-sweep-b|statement=Interior: a duplicate function is not thrown away - it is self-identifying, its address already exists, so storing it again is a no-op costing zero marginal bytes. Outward: THE ADDRESS IS THE DEDUP - no deletion is ever needed for dedup. Corollary a machine must instrument: d(store)/dt = surprise rate; d(savings)/dt = law-reuse rate. AGENT-written, drawn from the code, dated 2026-07-20; Book I contains and references none of this set.|json=0
LAW|n=Function Law 2 (VIII.C)|name=The Composable Verification Law|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=second-sweep-b|statement=Interior: a node is green iff its own reported value equals the watcher's recomputed value AND every child is green. Outward: verification COMPOSES UPWARD; it does not average - a machine must never roll up a mean to declare a tree green.|json=0
LAW|n=Function Law 3 (VIII.C)|name=The False-Down Law|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=second-sweep-b|statement=Interior: a failed observation is a property of the (observer, route) pair, not of the object - a degraded vantage reduces I(X ; observation); it cannot touch H(X). Outward: the formal form of the operator law of vantage (VIII.F.4) - absence from one vantage is a BOUNDARY, not a refutation; a machine must report the boundary, never a negative existence claim.|json=0
LAW|n=Function Law 4 (VIII.C)|name=The Two-Regime Collision Law|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=second-sweep-b|statement=Interior: EXECUTION lanes make collisions impossible-to-express by construction; SEARCH lanes CAUSE collisions on purpose - the interference peak IS the many->1 answer. Outward: collision is a bug in one regime and the mechanism in the other, so which regime you are in MUST BE DECLARED before a collision is judged.|json=0
LAW|n=Function Law 5 (VIII.C)|name=The Held-Potential Law|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=second-sweep-b|statement=Interior: freeze is not broken - a held-safe lane is an UNAPPLIED BIJECTION, H fully intact, loss impossible to express, advancing only on input BY DESIGN. Outward: the missing justification for Law 15 - a machine must not report a frozen lane as damaged, stalled or absent.|json=0
LAW|n=IV.1|name=Honest accounting|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim: the decoder is part of the payload. Outward: a machine must compute `bpc_total = (payload + decoder_src) × 8 / N` with `decoder_src` read at run time via `fs::metadata` and NEVER hard-coded, and every run must print `restore=OK` — 'a run without a restore line is not a result', so such a run must be discarded, not reported.|json=0
LAW|n=IV.2|name=The byte-frozen law|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim: a receipt must describe a program that still exists. Outward: while a job runs, its source file stays byte-frozen; a new arm must FORK the `.rs` / `.py` to a new filename; a live file is never edited. A machine that edits a running arm's source has voided that arm's receipt.|json=0
LAW|n=IV.3|name=The corpus-identity rules|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim: identity is by hash, not by size. Outward, four hard rules: (1) every measured row must name its corpus; (2) two files of the same length are not the same file; (3) a cross-arm comparison is VOID unless the corpus sha matches on both sides; (4) reproduce any logged baseline before trusting it — including your own. Extension added 2026-07-27, to prose: a number nobody on this seat measured gets the name of whoever measured it attached, or it does not get quoted (applied in `/root/manifest/CONTAINER-M|json=0
LAW|n=IV.4|name=The shipped-prior law (with ERRATA-1)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim: return on a shipped prior decays faster than its cost grows. Measured return rates 18.24%, 7.49%, 3.41%, 1.18%, fitting saving ∝ S^0.603; break-even requires saving ≥ S, which holds only below about 44 bytes. Outward: a machine must not ship a distant prior of any useful size into a SINGLE MONOLITHIC STREAM — it does not pay for itself. Refutation kept in the same entry: under SECTIONING it DOES pay, because the saving is a fixed transient per cold model start and so recurs every section while the c|json=0
LAW|n=IV.5|name=The contexts-per-byte screen|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim: counting distinct frozen order-2 contexts per training byte predicts a prior's worth BEFORE any compressor runs, and the correlation runs backwards — context count is ANTI-correlated with usefulness. Measured: KEY 0.160, ADJACENT 0.176, RANDOM 0.978, BIG 0.008. Outward: a machine must run this O(n) screen on the prior alone — no corpus, no compressor run — and prefer LOW contexts-per-byte priors, spending runs only on what survives the screen.|json=0
LAW|n=IV.6|name=The freeze-then-address principle|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim (Law 15 made operational for this seat): train once, then freeze the functions AND the fraction-of-a-rime addresses. Outward: after the freeze a machine plays with the Fischer in O(1) WITHOUT materializing, and the observer stays outside, at the null 0. Materializing in order to address is a violation, not an optimization.|json=0
LAW|n=IV.7|name=Held bytes are paid bytes|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim, forced by a contradiction the operator caught in one sentence of the seat's own prose ('it never enters the stream, and both sides must hold the same 3,174 bytes'): if both sides must HOLD it, it was SHIPPED. Outward: 'not in the stream' is not the same as 'free' — moving a payload out of the stream and into the decoder puts it exactly where Hutter counts it. A prior both sides must hold is CHARGED; calling it a key does not change the ledger. Corollary a machine must enforce: a folder named `key/` |json=0
LAW|n=IX.0 · field census over 5,837 user-role records|name=origin.kind == "human" is a field, not a heuristic|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: of 5,837 user-role records, 1,970 are isSidechain subagent prompts this seat wrote, 33 are task-notification, 4,947 carry no origin field, and 852 carry origin.kind == "human". Outward: a machine must filter operator voice by that field and never by role alone — filtering by role produced 990 "operator turns" including a 229,587-byte prompt beginning "You are the synthesis agent for a 40-scout fan-out" that this seat had written. The census cut 990 to 850 and the 140 removed are recorded as a mistake, not|json=0
LAW|n=IX.0 · method failure recorded|name=A result that exists only in a context window is not a result|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: the first fan-out returned its findings in the conversation and they were lost before being written to disk. Outward: agents write to disk FIRST (/root/manifest/mine/slice-NN.tsv) and return only a count; nothing may depend on anything held in a conversation.|json=0
