LAW|n=IX.B.1 · turn [0698] · voice-08.md:129|name=The translucent is free, the three colours are priced|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "The translucent space is the free data. The red, the blue, and the green are the data that costs." Outward: a machine must split any colour representation into a priced set (R,G,B) and a free set, and must never charge budget, storage or compute against the translucent register. Any cost model that prices all four waves alike is wrong at the root.|json=0
LAW|n=IX.B.2 · turn [0712] · voice-08.md:227|name=Two registers are never computed, and they carry the most|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "We don't have to calculate the zero and we don't have to calculate the translucent space. And that is what wins" / "translucent and zero are pro... probably contain more data than the the the three bits of red, blue, and green" / "we always thought there was a 2 bit balance but there is far more data". Outward: two of the five registers are skipped at evaluation time and they are the two with the highest information content; a machine must treat non-computation as the source of the advantage, not as an o|json=0
LAW|n=IX.B.3 · turn [0751] · voice-08.md:500|name=The five-value register: 0 zero, 1 translucent, 2 red, 3 green, 4 blue|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "The zero is the zero. The one is the translucent bit, and the two is the red" / "the three is the green, and the four is the blue". Outward: the base unit is FIVE-valued, not two-valued and not three-valued; a machine must index colour state 0..4 in that exact order, and translucent sits BETWEEN zero and the colours, not outside them. The traversal is stated as "you have to change back and forth from one bit to to two bits to three bits, and then the translucent bit" — i.e. widths change during the walk;|json=0
