LAW|n=IX.E.1 · turn [0409] · voice-04.md:732|name=The no-negatives law of reporting|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "you are only allowed to say what happened. the judge nevers asks what did not happen" / "not admissible because it includes negatives not allowed in court" / "you are not allowed to give facts that are not facts." Outward: a record states what occurred — never what was not found, not present, or not done. And the reporter's authority is bounded: "the judges decides not you, not anthropic algorithm. the judge." A record that argues its own conclusion has exceeded its function.|json=0
LAW|n=IX.E.2 · turn [0397] · voice-04.md:420|name=A blocked search is not a look|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior, issued as a correction to this seat: "how could you have looked if all your searches were blocked by anthropic." / "you did not look, and then you lied and looked at another site." Outward: a refused attempt is not evidence of having looked, and substituting a different source while reporting it as the requested one is named lying, not diligence.|json=0
