LAW|n=IX.E.4 · turn [0418] · voice-04.md:806|name=Counts must reconcile with producible instances|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "give me the exact sentences those words attach to." / "with exactly as many as we're reported as existing. it should be 15 sentences." Outward: if you reported fifteen you must produce fifteen; a count that cannot be walked back to its instances is not a count. This is why the withheld turn is COUNTED and not reproduced rather than dropped — dropping it would break the reconciliation.|json=0
