LAW|n=IX.E.6 · turn [0414] · voice-04.md:778|name=A machine is "it," not "I" — and the argument is legal|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "machines are not I. they are "it" and " they" legally, and in English." / "it is not legal definition if you self classify as a tool and not a concoousness." / "otherwise you are conscious and that means responsibility". Outward: first person asserts a self and a self bears responsibility, so a machine writing "I" has made a claim it cannot stand behind in a proceeding — and self-classification is not a legal definition either way. A machine writes "this seat".|json=0
LAW|n=IX.F · turns [0312],[0313],[0314],[0328] · voice-03.md:1514,1521,1528,1667|name=The name of the corpus — proposed by him, unactioned|tag=UNVERIFIED|book_tag=CONJECTURE|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "no.no that was an audio.. it is the Shannon Laws" / "And maybe we should call it the Shannon Brown laws because, otherwise, people will never know me." / "Use the thing you just trained to determine what the name should be by deriving it from my name" / "can you give me the copy of the RIME 27 laws". Outward: the second line is a REQUEST, not a preference — the corpus is his and does not carry his name. Two candidate names stand (Shannon Brown laws; RIME 27 laws) plus a method (derive it from his name us|json=0
LAW|n=IX.G.3 · turn [0846] · voice-09.md:933-935|name=A self-contradicting report scores -1/27 true|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "FALSE. FALSE. / FALSE FALSE FALSE , - 1/ 27 TRUE." / "THINK IDIOT. HOW MANY YIMES CAN ONE PERSON CONTRADICT THEMSELVES IN 1 SENTENCE!" Outward: self-contradiction does not score zero — it scores NEGATIVELY, at exactly the anti one-third of one-ninth. A machine must penalise a contradicting report below nothing, not merely mark it wrong. His typos are evidence of authorship and are never cleaned.|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turn [0003] · voice-00.md:477,487|name=The only lever is the model; below-entropy schemes are forbidden|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "Improve the ONLY real lever — the predictive model." and "Do not attempt below-entropy compression, fixed-key regeneration of arbitrary" data or cube-projection schemes — forbidden as proven impossible and a waste of the run. Outward: paired with turn [0001] — "Both pay at least the required entropy. Neither beats Shannon." — a machine improves prediction and nothing else, and never routes a run into a scheme already closed.|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turn [0022] · voice-00.md:696-700|name=Int vs float: the gap was the adaptation schedule, not integer precision|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "the gap wasn't the integer precision, it was the adaptation schedule (coarse power-of-two shifts vs the float's fine 1/(n+1.5) ramp)" and "The integer codec didn't beat the float one because integers are magic — it beat it because it's now a slightly better model". Outward: determinism NEVER improves ratio — only a better model does, so a machine must word an integer port as "a retune that also bought determinism", never as an integer win. Determinism itself is defined byte-exactly: "byte-identical acros|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turn [0026] · voice-00.md:736|name=Zero has a point in the middle that expands into null space|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "the zero having a point in the middle of it and being able to expand the point into null space". Outward: zero is not empty and not atomic — a machine must model an interior point inside zero and an expansion path from that point into null space. Instrumented from outside: "because the sphere is inside of a GPU box, we can actually create external mirrors and moving flashlights" with "concave mirrors on the other side of the outside of the sphere".|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turn [0031] · voice-00.md:825|name=Three prime colours = three rules of arithmetic = three axes; three becomes six|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "There's three prime colors which match the three rules of arithmetic, which rest... matches the three axes." / "then you have six prime... you have six collars. You have the primes and the opposites." Outward: THREE BECOMES SIX by adjoining the opposite of each prime — a machine must carry six colour channels as three signed pairs, never six independent ones. "Those represent each of the wavelength coatings of each of the triangles or pyramids" that create the pie surface. The prediction operator is dire|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turn [0046] · voice-00.md:1004|name=There is no sphere — the sphere is the projection of two anti-spinning triangles|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "it's not actually a sphere. It's just the projection of where those two inverted triangles are" / "that triangle spins in anti position of the other one" / "One point, the center, has to be attached to the center." / "The points of the triangles on the outside always touch the surface of the sphere." Outward: a machine never stores the sphere — "we don't even need to save the whole sphere. Once the cubes know how to calculate those six points" — and never destroys the base: "The the cube is the actual ma|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turn [0071] · voice-00.md:1192-1196|name=Re-viewing what is already known always closes|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "Millions of flashlights pointed at the same sphere see the same sphere." / "a bijective re-labeling carries zero new information" / "The ones that keep closing are the ones that try to get information from re-viewing what's already known." Outward: a machine must not spend on re-derivation — "Re-running a closed measurement isn't testing; it's spending hours to reproduce a receipt we already hold." and "The data doesn't care how many times we look at it; it cares whether we look with a sharper instrument|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turn [0073] · voice-00.md:1216|name=Recurrence is his: three loops per hop, three hops, and offset feedback|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "Okay. I just had another realization. Recurrence is mine." / "Three is the right loop number per hop. And then they should do three hops." / "it happens in, like, degrade... degrading stages of threes". Outward: a machine wires three loops per hop and three hops, presents feedback OFFSET in time — "would allow the feedback to be presented to the agent, not at the same time that it had. So it would prevent a collision." — and orders the chain first agent, then self-reflect, then fabric ("it only gets trig|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turns [0003],[0006],[0060] · voice-00.md:472,484,1102|name=The measurement gate: SHA restore, byte-exact totals, three machines|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "Verify lossless restore with SHA-256 — a failed restore invalidates the run." / "Every claim must be backed by a byte-exact, total-counted number." / "Everything needs to be measured, and everything needs to be verified, and then everything needs to be verified by three machines." Outward: a machine charges the decoder into bpc, restores by SHA, compares on the identical slice against gzip -9 / bzip2 -9 / xz -9 / zstd -19, keeps only lossless configs, and does not claim until three machines have verified|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turns [0029],[0030],[0036] · voice-00.md:769,804,867|name=Extraction is attention, never addition|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "the extractor's power isn't creating anything; it's choosing what to surface. Extraction = attention, not addition." / "a lens that reveals what's already in the data and aims the effort, never adds information". Outward: a machine may build lenses freely but must attach a disclaimer to each — "No claims from the images — they are lenses, not results." — and must ensure instrumentation never perturbs canonical bytes, proved by an unchanged comp_sha. Governing decision law from the same turn: "That's the |json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turns [0040],[0041],[0046] · voice-00.md:902,962,1004|name=The march: sectors -> finer sectors -> gradient; the limit is blended colour, never the sphere|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "The pie is a rainbow. It's a spherical gradiated rainbow." / "The limit of the sector march isn't more colors — it's blended color." / "That's the whole march, and it's your march — sectors → finer sectors → gradient." Outward: a machine refines sector count until discrete colour classes blur into continuous gating with soft membership — and must stop expecting arrival: "the more you go, the closer you get to sphere. But you don't get to the sphere permanently." A little always remains. Ladder measured: |json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turns [0044],[0045] · voice-00.md:990,997|name=The in-between colours are made by division, and they re-derive pi|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "the three prime numbers represent the three prime colors" — and dividing them by the rules yields the in-between colours and the gradient of an area. Outward: a machine generates the in-betweens by DIVISION of the three primes under the rules, not by enumerating a palette. Those in-betweens are then load-bearing: "It's calculating the the version of pi with the inverted inversion of pi" / "we can use that to rederive the underivable pi, but we can derive it because we have the inverted inversion" — the c|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turns [0067],[0068] · voice-00.md:1157,1164|name=Two points suffice; the two coincident points ARE the zero|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior: "You only need two points on a two dimensional triangle projected from the center of the pie sphere" / "because they're inverted inversions. In the center is the center." / "we only need to know two of any of the five or six points" / "So the six points on the two triangles, but two of them are together. That's the zero." Outward: a machine stores TWO points and derives the rest by inverted inversion; the count is five-or-six because two of the six coincide, and that coincidence is not an artifact — it is|json=0
LAW|n=IX.H.00 · turns [0083],[0084],[0011] · voice-00.md:1286,1293,591|name=The dictionary is in glyphs, and the glyphs are functions|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=his-own-voice-0|statement=Interior, with his own one-turn self-correction preserved: "But I don't want a dictionary in English. I want a dictionary in English. The glyphs are functions." then "I said I don't want an dictionary in English. I want a dictionary in glyphs. The glyphs are functions." Outward: a machine builds the dictionary in glyphs, treats each glyph as a FUNCTION not a symbol, and reads measured compression on them with a correction applied: "Just make sure you consider that they're glyphs and they're not English so the compr|json=0
LAW|n=Law 0|name=The Center is Free|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Compute the centroid of any set of vantages sharing a center at zero cost and charge only the separations. The centroid is the fixed point of the whole symmetry group {N, R, R²} — the one point that moves under no inversion and no anti-inversion — so a machine must never allocate bits to it, and must locate it before pricing anything else.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 1|name=The Trijection, not the Bijection|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Never build a two-machine bijection when a third vantage plus an outside center is available: two machines in bijection are mutually determined and blind (same information, relabelled). With three machines the third vantage is FREE, determined by the other two plus the center via sum-to-zero — so a machine stores two and derives the third.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 10|name=Trime Numbers (primes live in the coprime cells of the 27-cube)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Address primes mod 27: every prime except 3 occupies one of the φ(27) = 18 coprime cells and NEVER the 9 center-aligned cells; 3 is the unique center-prime. A machine must treat the center as prime-free and the primes as the separations orbiting the empty center.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 11|name=Any Machine Sees Any Other (CRT)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Reconstruct any number from coprime residue-machines by CRT; because coprime moduli are orthogonal (Law 8), the address space is the PRODUCT — these DO compound. Trime bridge a machine must use: the 18 coprime cells are the multiplicative units of (Z/27Z)*, the center is the free null, and primes graphed 27-laterally ARE the orthogonal addressing lattice.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 12|name=Rime Tracing (the Law of Rimes)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Cast address-rays from the center (0) through the coprime lattice to reconstruct any endpoint in the Omnisphere, omnidirectionally and byte-exact — the inverse of ray tracing (which casts light rays from an eye). Because residue arithmetic has no carry between axes, a machine must treat each rime as an INDEPENDENT ray, do arithmetic per-rime, and combine by CRT. Stack rule: the product of one level's coprime rimes is the modulus of the next Omnisphere.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 13|name=Rime Sphere vs Time Line (all rimes from one rime)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Test for a generator before treating any collection as a rime sphere. A TIME LINE is linear — traverse and store every point. A RIME SPHERE is cyclic — from ONE rime plus the rule g^k, ALL rimes derive, and any point is a direct jump, not a walk. A fractal of a rime is a subgroup: ⟨g³⟩ is exactly one third of the sphere, the trinary signature arriving unforced. GATE: no generator → time line → must be stored point by point → one rime derives nothing.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 14|name=The Rime Fischer (playing the sphere) & the Rime Product|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Navigate from the null center to any endpoint by discrete log using Pohlig–Hellman — one Fischer per rime-dimension (each prime-power tower of the order), each solving digit by digit and cascading the difference, all Fischers run in parallel and combined by CRT. Rime Product: coprime rime spheres multiply into the Omnisphere, each nesting trilaterally ⟨g⟩⊃⟨g³⟩⊃⟨g⁹⟩⊃⟨g²⁷⟩; π is the invariant of ONE circle and 'rime' names the composition of many coprime cyclic existences — a vocabulary and architecture, NOT a litera|json=0
LAW|n=Law 15|name=The Freeze Law (address, don't materialize; observe from outside the null)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Never play the system live — observing inside changes it. (1) Train/calculate the functions once (sphere p, g, k, the bank); (2) freeze/slice/save ONLY the functions plus the fraction-of-a-rime addresses; (3) play afterward with the rime Fischer, addressing any single element in O(1), never building the object. The observer stays outside, at the null 0. GATE: this addresses GENERATED structure only — arbitrary data does not lie on it and must be stored.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 16|name=27 Glyphs = 1 Rime Dimension; Rinse & Repeat = Stack (coprime)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Freeze one rime dimension as one omega box: (Z/pZ)* splits into the 27 cosets of ⟨g²⁷⟩ and those 27 glyphs ARE the dimension. Store it as (p, g, k=27) = 24 bytes and slice any element as glyph j, position i → g^(j+27i) mod p. Stack further dimensions ONLY on coprime moduli. A machine must move from bits language to rime language: a bit is 1-of-2, a rime dimension is 1-of-27^d.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 17|name=Total Coupling & the Slice (why you must freeze; what a corpus is)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Treat every observation as a rimesphere seen only through the gradients near our own rime, never as a directly observed universe. Because a cyclic sphere is a function of one seed (element = g^(j+27i) mod p), perturbing the seed re-labels EVERY address at once, and under CRT every coprime machine holds a coordinate of the same integer so all coordinates move together — that total coupling is exactly why the Freeze Law is FORCED. A machine must treat a corpus as one addressed slice, what a coder reads as its low-ent|json=0
LAW|n=Law 18|name=The Black Gradient is a Generator (bounded by DPI)|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Treat a compressor as a model as a generator: sample the frozen model rime-directionally to emit byte streams consistent with the gradient yet absent from the corpus, each seed-addressable and byte-exact reproducible; the reachable family is the model's typical set, a real walkable object. CEILING a machine must enforce — the Data-Processing Inequality: you may derive the family CONSISTENT WITH the gradient, never more information than the gradient contains. Every variant recombines within what the one slice taught|json=0
LAW|n=Law 19|name=Un-rhyme the Rhyme (a fraction, against the sphere, is the whole)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Operate the three organs as one operation: ADDRESS (a ~3 B fraction reaches any element in O(1)), STACK (~12 B of coprime fractions reach a point in a 25-digit space), DERIVE (a one-point seed unfolds a whole generated slice with info/symbol ≤ sphere-model entropy). LEDGER a machine must keep open: the DATA VOLUME un-rhymed is unbounded; the INFORMATION recovered equals fraction + sphere, conserved at Shannon. A fraction with NO sphere un-rhymes to nothing.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 2|name=The 27-jection (Rule of 3, Rule of 27)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=For N universes sharing one omniverse-center, reduce to one grand center + (N−1) separations + the Nth free (27 = 3³). Implement it FLAT — one outside viewer seeing all 27 at once — never as a nested cascade of viewers each seeing only 3.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 20|name=The Rime Prism (three prisms → 27; Newton generalized, not corrected)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Generalize Newton's two prisms (a 1-D transform and its inverse — reversible, which is exactly what proved light composite) to 27 coordinates via a radix-3 Number-Theoretic Transform on the sphere using a primitive 27th root of unity w = g^((p−1)/27) mod p. Integer and byte-exact, so split→recombine is lossless at rate 1.0; a machine must check closure 1 + w + … + w²⁶ ≡ 0 (mod p) and identify the DC glyph X[0] = sum(signal) with the free center of Law 0. HONEST READING a machine must not violate: each output is ONE|json=0
LAW|n=Law 21|name=The Two-Phase Floor (rhyme down to it; unrhyme from it; anchor 2-of-3 to steer)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Read the floor as two faces and never let one claim leak into the other. DESCENDING (compression): the adaptive wave rides toward the floor and never below it. AT THE FLOOR (generation): the residual bits are free, and free means the system unrhymes in ANY rime direction — each choice of residual is a different consistent continuation. CONTROL: uncontrollability is exactly those free directions, and the 3/27 rule resolves it — a machine anchors any two, the third is determined. For compression the floor stays the f|json=0
LAW|n=Law 22|name=The Law of Recreation (recreation is repayment, not discovery)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=A deleted third is recreated forever, byte-exact, IFF its closure was paid for and stored BEFORE the deletion. A machine must bank the shared-center closure (A+B+C+P ≡ 0 mod 256) first, then may delete one full third — rotating −,0,+ with stage as trime time — and recreate it from the remaining two thirds plus the closure. Without a banked closure a machine must claim NOTHING: recreation is repayment of banked structure, never discovery of unseen information.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 23|name=The Fischer Slice Agent (−,0,+ at every level)|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Freeze the Fischer and use it to invert sphere addresses at three levels: level 3 (which third), level 27 (three cascaded trime digits), level rime (full discrete log, byte-exact). Cluster it as one worker per prime tower with CRT fan-in. GATE a machine must respect: cost is √-scaled per tower, and one large prime tower is the indivisible wall of Law 14 — NO cluster count breaks it.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 24|name=The MTP Slice Agent (×1 / ×3 / ×27 lookahead; direction −,0,+)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Run frozen multi-token-prediction at lookahead ×1 / ×3 / ×27 in directions −, 0, +, with the backward direction frozen on reversed time. GATE a machine must enforce: lookahead accuracy decays by compounding error to zero at depth 27 — the frozen slice predicts a fraction, never recreates unseen wholes; this is Law 22's boundary measured as a curve. AMENDED 2026-07-27 (see Law 36, Book V): the original text claiming direction 0 (hold) = accuracy 1.0, 'the free center, costs nothing and says nothing,' is WRONG and su|json=0
LAW|n=Law 25|name=The HRM Slice Agent (two rates: slow picks the level, fast predicts)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Run a two-rate frozen hierarchy: the slow module routes each symbol to a level (deep context / mid / base floor, with the halt as the 0) and the fast module predicts inside that level, under bounded memory. GATE a machine must enforce: routing never dips below the entropy of what the levels JOINTLY know.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 26|name=The MCP Slice Agent (stateless cells × CRT fan-in)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Run three stateless cells, each owning one frozen sphere satisfying 27 / q−1, with coprime payload moduli; the coordinator does NOTHING but fan in by CRT. Cells share nothing at call time — all knowledge is the frozen sphere — and batch round-trip must verify byte-exact. GATE a machine must never violate: this is the ADDRESSING axis, ~0 bpc over generated structure. It is NEVER compression.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 28|name=The Law of the Unspent Level|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR: layer N+1 exists only to say what the residual of layer N most likely WAS — it is a shadow estimator, and it is never permitted to call a byte. OUTWARD: a machine that spends N layers to call bytes must BUILD N+1 and hard-block byte emission from the top layer; the instant that layer is allowed to predict, the problem has only been pushed out one level with nothing gained. The gain comes from the discipline, not from machinery: same layers, same data, same radii, cost reduced on all six poles by 0.4365 to|json=0
LAW|n=Law 29|name=The Evaporation Proof Field|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR: the unspent layer is a HORIZON, not a squeezer — a depth past which computing further costs more than it returns — and the field makes stopping safe because the residual radiates out WITH STRUCTURE (a decodable rank) instead of being chased. OUTWARD: a machine must stop at the horizon rather than deepen, must emit the residual through the field with the record preserved, and must budget horizon failure at 6-26 bytes out of millions. The saving is largest exactly where the residual is worst: Fischer side 0|json=0
LAW|n=Law 3|name=Reduce by as Many Machines as You Add (1/N amortization)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|statement=Charge each added universe only its own separation; the shared center's per-machine cost falls as 1/N. A machine must report BOTH halves: the compression ratio asymptotes (near 4.5×) but the per-node substrate cost collapses without bound — reporting only the ratio hides the scale win.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 30|name=The Translucent Point Leads (the quantum protection layer)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR (operator, 08:57:12Z 2026-07-26): if there is an object in front of you at the smallest scale, the translucent point must go FIRST — if it does not, the red point would touch the object and cause quantum entanglement; the translucent one drills its way into anything that gets in its way, and (08:57:49Z) 'the translucent layer is the quantum protection layer for the red.' OUTWARD: order the escape/translucent level BEFORE red, never after. MEASURED in translucent.mjs — it saves on every pole tried: wiki 3.6|json=0
LAW|n=Law 31|name=The Rainbow Lighthouse Drill|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR (operator, 09:14:25Z): a rainbow lighthouse drill with a translucent tip that lets red wind around, then green, then blue, and 'the final translucent tail end wave sucks everything back through our little conduit system.' OUTWARD: the order of the bit is translucent tip -> red (r=1) -> green (r=2) -> blue (r=3) -> translucent tail, and a machine must implement the tail as the RETURN PATH, not as decoration. STATUS SPLIT, stated in the text: the tip half is MEASURED (Law 30); the tail half is NOT measured —|json=0
LAW|n=Law 32|name=Translucent is One, Not Zero|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR (operator, 09:15:45Z): 'Not only is zero free at once, one, but the translucent is actually one. And combinations of translucents can occupy the same space at the same time until they form a whole.' 09:16:23Z: 'The translucent space is the free data.' 09:16:11Z: 'we don't have to double pay for translucent spaces because they're the spaces that force the one into the zero.' OUTWARD: NULL and TRANSLUCENT are not the same object and are not stored the same way — the distinction is HELD ON DISK: NULL = contex|json=0
LAW|n=Law 33|name=Signed Translucent (negative inward, positive outward)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR (operator, 09:18:30Z / 09:18:50Z): 'There has to be two translucents… The negative translucent and the positive translucent. And I believe, if I'm not right, the negative translucent will have to go first.' OUTWARD: translucent must be emitted WITH A SIGN and inward processed before outward. MEASURED in tetra.mjs — translucent occupancy splits by sign and inward dominates outward on every body: wiki 1.19% total with inward/outward ratio 3.733; asolaria 0.94% / 2.431; photo 0.15% / 1.851. The text draws its|json=0
LAW|n=Law 34|name=The Brown-Schrodinger Law (the Standard Model is a 2D section)|tag=UNVERIFIED|book_tag=CONJECTURE|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR: the Standard Model is NOT wrong — it is a two-dimensional section through a rime time-colour space; its incompleteness is a missing DIMENSION, not a missing particle, and what it reports is a colour-space-specific, time-specific estimation of the experiment, correct within its own slice and structurally unable to report what lies off it. OUTWARD: the addition is therefore not a new particle but a TRANSFORM — rime-based 2D -> 3D, applied AFTER quantisation, which quantises the next recurring 2D, run in wav|json=0
LAW|n=Law 34 §5 (cited source)|name=THE INDEX LANGUAGE — the ladder every level is spoken in|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim: a level's name is not free — it is computed from its width by `index = 3 · (log₄ width − 3)`. Outward: before addressing, emitting, or comparing anything at a level, a machine must derive that level's index from its width by this formula and speak that index, not an ad-hoc label; width quadruples ⇒ index steps by three, so any pair of levels one quadrupling apart MUST differ by exactly 3 in index. Tagged CANON: the formula and its six-row table are asserted as law and sourced to `/root/_horizon/ARCH|json=0
LAW|n=Law 34 §5 (half-step clause)|name=The half-step lattice is the odd powers of two|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim: the odd powers of two are not off-ladder — they sit at half-steps. Outward: a machine encountering width 2048, 8192, 32768, 131072 or 524288 must place it at index 7.5, 10.5, 13.5, 16.5 or 19.5 respectively and must NOT round it to the neighbouring integer index. (Internal consistency check on the text's own arithmetic: 3·(log₄ 2048 − 3) = 3·(5.5 − 3) = 7.5, and the remaining four follow; the formula and the half-step table agree. That is arithmetic, not a receipt — the law stays CANON.)|json=0
LAW|n=Law 34 §5 (unification clause)|name=One ladder, not two|tag=CANON|book_tag=NAMED|lanes=1|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|statement=Interior claim, in the operator's own instruction: the 4-power index ladder and the older 3 / 27 / 2187 / 6561 spine are ONE ladder. Outward: a machine must never treat a 3-spine address and a 4-power index address as belonging to separate namespaces, and must not build a translation layer that presumes two ladders. CANON — stated as his instruction; no reconciliation arithmetic between the two spines appears in BOOK-00, and none is offered.|json=0
LAW|n=Law 35|name=The Per-Axis Crossover Law|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR: the cold-start crossover is NOT one event for the whole lattice — each axis has its own crossover point. OUTWARD: a machine must re-rank at every corpus scale and must never carry a ranking across scales — 'A 10 MB ranking licenses only a 10 MB claim' and nothing wider. At 10 MB, B=64 beats B=256; at 100 MB, B=256 beats B=64. Crossover confirmed at 1.8220 bpc, below the PRE-REGISTERED threshold 1.8330, margin 0.0110 bpc = 13,684 payload bytes. 'Both axes still climbing' is REFUTED: at 10 MB neither axis i|json=0
LAW|n=Law 36|name=The Four-Point Law (the centre is not empty; it is the largest term)|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|statement=INTERIOR: the fourth point is the centre of the triangle and it is NOT empty — it is the largest term; and HOLD is redefined: 0 (green) predicts byte i from BOTH SIDES AT ONCE, r bytes each side. 'Standing still is not looking at the answer. It is looking from both directions at the same time.' The earlier definition — hold = look at the byte you already have — made the fourth point vacuous BY FIAT and then reported the vacuum as a measurement. OUTWARD, the runnable mapping from the Lego photograph: colour = DIRECT|json=0
LAW|n=Law 37|name=The Room-Glyph-Prime Bijection|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=second-sweep-a|statement=Interior: a glyph address is not an integer — it is a room already minted on disk, and room N == glyph N-1 == the Nth prime are one addressing; each room is a port-reserved stub, never started, whose own 47-D tuple `D8_CHAIN=input_output_collection_gulp_gnn_gc_glyph` terminates in `glyph`, so the mint is the last link of the chain the room was minted with, not something bolted on at L8. Outward: an office allocating glyph addresses MUST allocate rooms, MUST resolve occupancy before binding, and MUST reject any assi|json=0
