LAW|n=Law 38|name=The Thirty-Four Tongues|tag=MEASURED|book_tag=MEASURED|lanes=1|lane=second-sweep-a|statement=Interior: every body's surface codebook is a permutation of the 1024 glyphs seeded by that body's own sha256 — `never_english=1` is a law, not an omission — and translation between tongues is a receipted permutation: exact, reversible, no semantics in the middle, with two tongues predicting the same body agreeing exactly up to tie-break. Outward: a machine MUST translate by identity-permutation and never by an English pivot or a shared surface codebook (English translates by approximation and loses); MUST use the `|json=0
