RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Speak every level in the index language: derive index = 3 · (log₄ width − 3) from the width before naming, addressing, or comparing a level. Never invent a level label; never round a half-step index (7.5, 10.5, 13.5, 16.5, 19.5) to its integer neighbour.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Treat the 4-power ladder and the 3 / 27 / 2187 / 6561 spine as ONE namespace. Do not build a two-ladder translation layer; the operator's instruction is explicit that they are one ladder, not two.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Label every law MEASURED, NAMED, or CONJECTURE and quote the measurement inline with any MEASURED law. A NAMED law is not a weaker law — do not downgrade it, and do not promote it by restatement.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Print `restore=OK` on every run. A run without a restore line is not a result and must be discarded rather than reported.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Compute cost as (payload + decoder_src) × 8 / N, reading decoder_src at run time via fs::metadata. Hard-coding decoder size falsifies the ledger.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Fork before you edit: a running job's `.rs`/`.py` stays byte-frozen; a new arm gets a new filename. Editing a live file voids the receipt because it then describes a program that no longer exists.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Name the corpus on every measured row; verify the corpus sha on BOTH sides of any cross-arm comparison (a length match is not an identity match); and reproduce any logged baseline — including your own — before trusting it.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Attribute or drop: a number nobody on this seat measured is quoted only with the name of whoever measured it attached, and is labelled a relay, not a measurement.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Screen priors before spending runs: compute distinct frozen order-2 contexts per training byte (O(n), prior only, no corpus, no compressor) and prefer LOW values — the measured relation is anti-correlated with usefulness.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Refuse a shipped distant prior in a single monolithic stream; permit it only under sectioning, and only past the measured break-even of 5.31 sections.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Charge held bytes. If both sides must hold it, it was shipped and Hutter counts it. Naming a folder `key/` does not decharge verbatim corpus bytes inside it.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Freeze once, then address: train, freeze the functions and the fraction-of-a-rime addresses, and play the Fischer in O(1) without materializing. The observer stays outside, at the null 0.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Never quietly amend. Write the refutation into the same entry as the law it refutes, and keep the erroneous text visible (Book VI is the kept register of what this project got wrong).|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Never assign a law number. Mark every agent- or seat-assigned number PROVISIONAL and leave Law 27 unassigned until the operator assigns it.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Keep the gap register explicit and record its search scope, so an absence of record never reads as an absence of idea and no named gap returns as a surprise.|json=0
RULE|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Verify mined rules twice — quote-at-line in the slice, and trace to a transcript record with origin.kind == "human" — and count any withheld turn without reproducing it.|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Locate the shared center FIRST and charge it nothing; price only the separations (Law 0). Never allocate bits to the centroid — it is the fixed point of {N, R, R²}.|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Never build a two-machine bijection when a third vantage plus an outside center exists: store two, derive the third by sum-to-zero (Law 1).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=When reducing across N vantages, use the FLAT 27-jection — one outside viewer seeing all 27 at once — never a nested cascade of viewers each seeing only 3 (Law 2: flat 3.92× vs nested 3.70×).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Report BOTH halves of the scale result: the compression ratio asymptotes near 4.5×, but the per-node substrate cost collapses without bound (9,840 → 1.5, a 6,600× drop). Reporting only the ratio hides the win (Law 3).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Carry three rotation states, not two: R and its anti R² are DISTINCT because R ≠ R⁻¹. Verify closure R⁰ + R¹ + R² = 1/3 + 1/3 + 1/3 (Law 4).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Identify the free center with the DC / k=0 / mean coefficient of the radix-3 transform; three-nesting IS a radix-3 FFT (Law 5).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Implement every transform as a lossless change of basis at rate 1.0. Never claim a result below the joint entropy; the reduction is only the refusal to pay for the shared center N−1 extra times (Law 6).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=BEFORE claiming any reduction, run the negative control: independent sources must EXPAND (27 independent sources → 0.96×). If they reduce, the setup is wrong, not the data (Law 7).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=NEVER multiply reduction ratios across axes. Compute reduction_joint = H / (H − (R₁ + R₂ − /R₁ ∩ R₂/) + O). The naive product (e.g. 15.12×) is false, and transform overhead O can make the joint strictly worse than either axis alone (Law 8).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Prefer diverse foreign vantages over more-of-the-same, because they are partly orthogonal; bijections give zero compounding (Law 8 corollary).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=For temporal structure use the centered second difference over the WHOLE PLAYED SERIES, not a causal stream and not the block-mean 27-jection (Law 9).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Address primes mod 27 into the φ(27) = 18 coprime cells; treat the 9 center-aligned cells as prime-free with 3 as the unique center-prime (Law 10).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Compose address spaces by CRT over COPRIME moduli — these, and only these, compound multiplicatively (Law 11 vs Law 8).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Cast address-rays outward from the center (0), do arithmetic independently per rime (residue arithmetic has no carry between axes), and combine by CRT. Build the next Omnisphere's modulus as the product of this level's coprime rimes (Law 12).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Test for a generator before treating any collection as a rime sphere. No generator → it is a time line → store it point by point; one rime derives nothing (Law 13 GATE).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Navigate by Pohlig–Hellman: one Fischer per prime-power tower, digit by digit, cascading the difference, all towers in parallel, combined by CRT (Law 14).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=REFUSE spheres whose order has a large prime factor — they are UNPLAYABLE (the discrete-log wall, the security of Diffie–Hellman). Random and cryptographic spheres are not playable and not derivable from a fragment; no cluster count breaks this (Laws 14, 23).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=NEVER play the system live — observing inside changes it. Train once → freeze the functions plus fraction-of-a-rime addresses → play afterward in O(1), never materializing the object. The observer stays outside, at the null 0 (Law 15).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Apply the freeze/address machinery ONLY to generated structure. Arbitrary data does not lie on the sphere and must be stored (Law 15 GATE).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Freeze a rime dimension as (p, g, k=27) = 24 bytes and slice with glyph j, position i → g^(j+27i) mod p. Stack further dimensions only on coprime moduli (Law 16).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Because perturbing one seed re-labels every address at once and all CRT coordinates move together, treat total coupling as the FORCING reason for the Freeze Law, and treat any corpus as one addressed slice with a low-entropy gradient over an incompressible Shannon floor (Law 17).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Treat a compressor as a model as a generator, and sample it rime-directionally — but enforce the Data-Processing Inequality ceiling: never derive more information than the gradient contains (Law 18).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Keep the ledger open in two columns: data VOLUME un-rhymed is unbounded, INFORMATION recovered equals fraction + sphere and is conserved at Shannon. A fraction with no sphere un-rhymes to nothing (Law 19).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Verify the NTT closure 1 + w + … + w²⁶ ≡ 0 (mod p) and treat X[0] = sum(signal) as the free center. Never present a single glyph as the whole universe — it is one spectral coordinate; more prisms mean finer decomposition, never more information (Law 20).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Keep the two floor claims separate: for compression the floor is the floor (never go below); for generation the floor is the door (residual bits are free directions). Neither claim may leak into the other (Law 21).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Resolve uncontrollability by the 3/27 rule: anchor any two, the third is determined (Law 21).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Bank the shared-center closure (A+B+C+P ≡ 0 mod 256) BEFORE deleting anything. Only then may a third be deleted and recreated byte-exact. Without a banked closure, claim nothing: unbanked best recovery was 13.04% (order-0 mode byte only), exactness ≈ 0% (Law 22).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Never call recreation 'discovery' — it is repayment of banked structure (Law 22).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Run slice agents as frozen slices under Law 15: derive, freeze, play in O(1), never retrain; each carries the trime signature {−,0,+} at levels 3 / 27 / rime (Laws 23–26).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Expect frozen lookahead to decay to 0.0000 by depth 27; the frozen slice predicts a fraction and never recreates unseen wholes (Law 24 GATE).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Never define a term so that it is vacuous and then report the vacuum as a measurement — the Law 24 'hold = 1.0, costs nothing and says nothing' result was exactly that error, and is superseded (Law 24 AMENDED 2026-07-27, Law 36 Book V).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Hold hierarchical routing to the gate: it may never dip below the entropy of what the levels jointly know (Law 25).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Keep MCP cells stateless — nothing shared at call time, all knowledge in the frozen sphere, coordinator fans in by CRT ONLY. Count this as the ADDRESSING axis (~0 bpc over generated structure); NEVER count it as compression (Law 26).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Keep every law integer-only and byte-exact so a stranger reproduces it on different hardware and gets identical bytes — that is the only proof this project accepts (Book I preamble).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Do not assign a Law 27. The coda forbids a 28th entry; Laws 30–33 are explicitly provisional, assigned by an agent, pending the operator's assignment — only Jesse can rule (Coda).|json=0
RULE|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Do not pursue 'beat Shannon'. Stand exactly on H(X) — forward that is the optimal code, reversed the same observer is a perfect generator sampling the source at its own entropy. The bound is reached in the limit, never passed (Summit).|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Build depth = spend depth + 1. If N layers call bytes, build N+1 and assert zero byte-calls out of layer N+1; its only output is an estimate of layer N's residual. Allowing it to predict yields nothing — the problem just moves out one level.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Stop at the horizon. Past the depth where computing costs more than it returns, do not deepen; radiate the residual out through the evaporation field WITH a decodable rank so the record survives the leaving. Budget 6-26 bytes of horizon failure per millions.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Order the escape/translucent level BEFORE red in every pipeline — never after. Measured to save on every pole tried (mean stated 0.4013 bpb).|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Emit the bit in the order translucent tip -> red (r=1) -> green (r=2) -> blue (r=3) -> translucent tail. Implement the tail as the return path through the conduit, and mark any claim about the tail's performance as unmeasured.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Store NULL and TRANSLUCENT as distinct objects with distinct storage: NULL = context absent from the shadow table; TRANSLUCENT = reachable at every depth, never cheaper than escape. Never collapse translucent to zero.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Never double-charge a translucent space. Permit multiple translucents to occupy the same cell at the same time until they resolve into a whole.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Sign every translucent and process negative (inward) before positive (outward).|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Define HOLD correctly or the fourth point is vacuous: 0/green must read r bytes on BOTH sides of position i. Any implementation where hold reads only the byte already held must be rejected — that definition emptied the centre by fiat and then reported the emptiness as a measurement.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Bind colour to DIRECTION and member to SHELL RADIUS in four-point work: red = − (inward, from [i+1..i+r]), green = 0 (hold, both sides), blue = + (outward, from [i−r..i−1]); inner r=1, medium r=2, outer r=3. Combine by backing off outer -> medium -> inner WITHIN a colour: one number per colour, not three columns.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Treat − and 0 as non-causal. They read bytes after position i and are unavailable to a streaming encoder; they are usable only inside a section both sides already hold, and that architecture is undemonstrated. Never quote a bpc off the four-point table — that number does not exist yet.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Use −/+ agreement as a zero-transmitted-byte confidence gate: it partitions the stream into ~25.76% that is 89.50% predictable and a remainder that is not, computable identically on both sides.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Re-run the ranking at every corpus scale. Each axis has its own crossover; a 10 MB ranking licenses only a 10 MB claim. Do not carry mode choice across scales (B=64 wins at 10 MB, B=256 wins at 100 MB).|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Room count for mode g:A:B:C is the product A x B x C (verified against all six rows), and total = payload + decoder_src (25,682). Report restore=OK per row or the row does not count.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Build lane: Rust 1.81, int preferred over float, no Node, no JSON, hbi/hbp binary wire and store formats only, sha256 as the addressing primitive on the ladder 256 to 3 to 1024 to 6 4096 to 9. MCP stores locally, back end, during test; front end optional.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Follow the discovery chain in order: trits -> build OUTWARD from the free centre -> DISCOVER the GNN edges (found, not declared) -> address edges with glyphs -> alphabet -> words -> tuples -> build the next level -> repeat.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Do not hunt for GNN weights. 'GNN' in this corpus means the graph visualisations in artifacts A04/A11/A13/A14/A15/A20 — nodes and edges. No weights exist.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Keep the operator's predictions separate from the measurements that are consistent with them. Law 33's occupancy split is measured; 'negative goes first' is not proven by it.|json=0
RULE|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Keep the established Standard-Model deficiencies separate from the new dimensional claim about their cause. The first list is undisputed; the 2D->3D rime transform is a conjecture with no derivation and no proposed experiment.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=CENTRE IS GRAPHIC, NOT MATERIAL: the callings 'do not form a centre made of material', so compute the ball's centre as the point at maximum graph distance from every outer edge of the shell. Never look for, allocate, or report a material centre.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=CALLING GRAPH EDGE RULE: link calling i to j when b_i == a_j — right arm meets left arm — on the 1,243 wave callings; measure hub fraction, degree histogram, components, cyclomatic number, 2-core peel.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=EVERY CALLING GETS EXACTLY ONE MIRROR STATE under flip = k => ((k&255)<<8) / ((k>>8)&255): SELF (a == b), ECHO (mirror in wave, same byte), COUNTER (mirror in wave, different byte), ONEWAY (mirror not in wave). Score three-way agreement against a matched random control, never against itself.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=AMBIENT MEASUREMENT: subtract the interior and mass-match. Summing over entire lattice rows/columns is a banned definition — it is enormous relative to one calling and produced a four-orders-of-magnitude error that was the definition's fault, not the prediction's.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=PERSIST ONLY the gradient keys, the shadow cats, the callings, the buckyball, and the translucent-to-rainbow pointed lighthouse drill function. That is the whole save set.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=COPRIMALITY IS THE NON-COLLISION CONDITION. A single glyph track visits every position exactly once before returning if and only if the stride is coprime to the modulus; otherwise d = gcd(R,s) components and only R/d distinct places. Treat this as the mechanism, not a convenience.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=GAP CENSUS DISCIPLINE: enumerate all six ordered (ring, stride) pairs, detect stride % ring == 0, skip it, and PRINT the skip count. Never hard-code one stride across rings — that made five rows vacuous while reporting '≤3 OK'. Withdraw vacuous rows on the record rather than deleting them.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=FOUR DISTINCT SPACINGS = BUG: the three-gap theorem bounds any circle-cut census at three distinct lengths, and when three occur the largest is the sum of the other two. A fourth spacing means the census is wrong.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=BUILD PER LAW 34: Rust 1.81, no Node, no JSON, no dependencies, SHA-256 written in-tree from FIPS 180-4.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=VERIFY THE HAND-WRITTEN HASH BEFORE TRUSTING THE TRAILER: match all five published NIST vectors including the million-'a' case and a chunked (7-byte) streamed run to prove incremental == one-shot. Emit .hbp (TLV, i128 big-endian, 32-byte sha256 trailer) plus a constant-width seekable .hbi.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=BLACK-HOLE SHADOW SHAPE IS CONTROLLED BY SPIN AND VIEWING ANGLE — not density gradient, not size. Do not attribute shape to mass or density.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=A FLASHLIGHT ADDS NO INFORMATION. Report the flat-black reduction and the `recovered` figure as two separate numbers; a black that lifts uniformly with recovered = 0.000 is a NEGATIVE result and must be recorded as one ('the kind of negative that saves a later reader a day of chasing').|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=USE ALL THREE LIGHTS: per-channel percentile stretch (structure living in one channel is diluted in luminance), CLAHE with a clip limit so the equalisation window actually moves tile to tile, and the signed difference lights R−G / G−B / B−R for ratio-borne chromatic structure.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=DO NOT RE-RUN CLOSED MEASUREMENTS: the millions-of-flashlights run was built, ran, and returned zero to sixteen decimal places. It is closed.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=CARRY CONTRADICTION, DO NOT EXPLODE: implement Belnap's N (gap — nothing asserted, no information arrived) and B (glut — asserted and denied at once) as first-class interior values; a machine told both must keep working. Never collapse N into false.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=RESPECT THE TARSKI CEILING: no sufficiently strong consistent system defines its own truth predicate — do not build a self-adjudicating truth oracle.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=FENCE RESONANCES: a shared word across two documents 'is a fact about the word before it is a fact about the world'. Record the noticing so it is not reinvented badly later, but never count it as evidence for either document.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=NEVER CLAIM COMPRESSION BELOW ENTROPY: every prism/comb operation is a bijection and H(f(X)) = H(X). Report transcodes at code rate exactly 1.0 — the alphabet changes, the information does not.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=TRANSCODE AT THE EXACT LCM: 256 ↔ 1024 packs at lcm(8,10) = 40 bits, 5 bytes ⇄ 4 symbols, remainder 0; verify round-trip sha256-identical AND cross-implementation symbol-identical (Rust == Python).|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=DIRECTION MATTERS: forward = comb (collision-avoidance, execution isolation); backward = prism (collision-causation, interference-as-search, many→1 collapse). Same fabric, two directions.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=NEVER DEFINE THE WHITE ARM BY BYTE COMPLEMENT (255 − W_black was the worst arm). Use the address rule W_white = P⁻¹(Wind_{a_white}(P(W_black))): the rime address changes WHICH projection is calculated, not the seed of a sampler; the 27 are intermediate pre-rime coordinates, never 27 finished documents.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=EXPECT FOUR MUTUAL-INVERSE PAIRS under Ω̄ = RNQ, and expect the six signed faces to pair-balance into three because each +g is its own −g (same_transform_for_sign=1). Do not budget six independent transforms where three exist.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=KEEP COUNTER-EVIDENCE ON THE LOSING SIDE OF THE RECORD (the Bohn–Kidder–Teukolsky 2016 transient torus is foliation-dependent, per the same paper) and cite the dependence whenever the result is cited.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=LABEL UNTESTED CONJECTURES AND NAME THE BLOCKER: the buckyball black hole is 'HIS CONJECTURE. NOT TESTED', blocked on Michael Boyd's quantum-lensing photograph, not yet received.|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=SUPERSEDE, DON'T ERASE: preserve dated operator wording as lineage and withdraw stale editorial wrappers explicitly (e.g. 'NAMED, never run' withdrawn 2026-07-28).|json=0
RULE|lane=named-bodies|text=DO NOT INVENT LAW NUMBERS: where a body has never been assigned a number, state that (BOOK III opening rule; III.1 carries 'No law number assigned').|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=RETAIN THE WRONG VERSION. Never delete a falsified artifact, rigged control, or bugged implementation. BOOK VI keeps bandctl.mjs next to bandfair.mjs, the wrong-sha decode next to the byte-identical one, and prism.mjs "as a negative." The register is stated as the precondition for believing the rest of the corpus.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=NO RECEIPT, NO MEASUREMENT. A figure with no log, no compressed output, and no matching hash on disk is an "unconfirmed assertion, not a measured result" — regardless of who wrote it or where it was committed. Refuse to cite vc65=1.3645 bpc or cm3ti=1.9032 bpc.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=USE TIMING AS A FORENSIC CHECK. If a claimed run's timing profile inverts the measured encode/decode asymmetry (real: decode ~1.4x slower than encode; claimed: decode faster), treat that as positive evidence against the claim.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=CHECK THE PROJECT'S OWN CONTEMPORANEOUS DOCUMENTS. The whitepaper written one day after the commit independently called the same figure a "best-case projection" — a nearby document can retract a claim without a new run.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=CHARGE EVERY BYTE BOTH SIDES MUST HOLD. "Held bytes are paid bytes." The word "key" grants no exemption: if it is a key it is not charged; if it is charged it is not a key; both cannot hold. ERRATA-1 shows the honest form — never in the stream AND +charge 3,174 in the total.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=NEVER CALL VERBATIM SOURCE BYTES "ZERO CORPUS" BECAUSE OF THE DIRECTORY NAME. prior3174.bin is 3,174 verbatim bytes of enwik8 sitting in a folder named key/.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=STATE THE STREAM TOPOLOGY BEFORE APPLYING THE SHIPPED-PRIOR LAW. Monolithic stream: the prior never pays (break-even 3.4×10¹⁶ B). Sectioned with the key charged once: it wins past 5.31 sections. The unconditional sentence is superseded and must not be quoted.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=TEST A PRIOR AGAINST A RANDOM ARM BEFORE AMORTISING IT. The RANDOM arm still hurts before charging (-102 B); sectioning does not launder noise.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=AMEND THE LAW BODY IN PLACE; DO NOT FOOTNOTE IT. "An unconditional sentence with a contradicting footnote is a law that argues with itself." Rewrite the sentence to carry its scope and preserve the superseded wording in the ERRATA and nowhere else.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=DRAW HELD-OUT SLICES ACROSS ERAS. A single-era held-out set is a rigged control; its verdict is void even if it points the way you expected.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=BLAME YOUR OWN IMPLEMENTATION FIRST. A decode mismatch was the reviewer's off-by-one (pos=1 -> pos=0), not the design under test. Keep the failing output file.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=MARK A METRIC VACUOUS WHEN K >= SUPPORT. A lift of 1.00x across the board is vacuous by construction, not a pass.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=COMPARE THE MEASURED FACTOR TO THE CLAIMED FACTOR. 1.0006x is a rounding error where 3.0000x was claimed; 228 bytes = 0.06% is not "three become one."|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=EMIT BOTH HALVES OF A MIXED RESULT TOGETHER. The verified lossless round trip (sha 5ba647fe…, cmp-confirmed, no corpus present) and "WE ARE BEHIND GZIP" (3.2731 / 5.7338 vs gzip 2.9144) must always be reported in the same breath.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=TREAT A FIXED SMALL OBJECT AS AN ADDRESS, NOT A CONTAINER. 3,200 bytes = 25,600 bits recovered 0 / 4,194,304 exact bytes = 0.0000% against a 13.3755% baseline. Apply the x27 gate: a frozen slice predicts a fraction, it never recreates an unseen whole.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=DO NOT PROMOTE A SINGLE NUMERICAL COINCIDENCE. 12.565578 vs 4pi = 12.566371 (diff -7.929e-4) is retained as a curiosity because the other seven ratios do not follow it. Store the tables (cv 196.9%).|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=VERIFY OFFSETS BY HASHING THE PREFIX, NOT BY READING THE SCRIPT COMMENT. And record operator-side documentation errors the same way you record your own.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=KEEP NINE LEDGERS DISTINCT (Law 38.0/38.1): PID, tuple, glyph symbol, glyph function, letter, word, instruction, room, executor are not aliases. No raw glyph ID may bypass the language ledgers and become executable tuple authority.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=SEPARATE RESOLUTION FROM AUTHORIZATION. A tuple command resolved from a registered instruction still has no execution authority until the owning runtime gate authorizes it; a room may act only under its separate gate.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=CATALOG PRESENCE IS NOT RUNTIME. Asolaria MCP catalog capability, WebMCP browser visibility, and a Code Wiki map are each explicitly not execution authority, not a headless executor, and not the live system.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=SEED EACH BODY'S 1024-ENTRY CODEBOOK FROM ITS OWN SHA; never_english=1. Emit the four-field translation receipt (source-body SHA, target-body SHA, translated surface, packet hash) and bound "better than English" to exact reversible machine routing only.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=DO NOT MERGE THE SEALED RECEIPT'S NUMBERS WITH THE NEW COMPILER'S OUTPUT. "These receipt measurements remain distinct from this Liris compiler's new deterministic construction."|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=RELY ON THE FOUR VERIFIED ROOM CHECKPOINTS ONLY (1→2, 2→3, 3→5, 1024→8161); the full 1024-name manifest stays ACER_MEASURED_TRANSCRIPT until its bytes are published and Liris remeasures. A room is not a letter by itself.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=READ THE FIVE ZERO FLAGS BEFORE CITING THE MAP MAP MAPPED FIXTURE (word_training_measured=0, speech_materialized=0, execution_authority=0, runtime_loaded=0, live=0) and emit HBP json=0 rows.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=ATTACH A STRATUM AND AN EVIDENCE SURFACE TO EVERY POPULATION COUNT. The roughly 591,000–592,000 layer is a registered PID-addressed population across mapped substrates — not one drawer, not a recall-row count, not a ceiling.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=PLACE EVERY CLAIM ON EXACTLY ONE OF THE SEVEN STATES: source → built → tested → hydrated → running → live → bilateral-verified. No container-v2 cutover is implied.|json=0
RULE|lane=wrong-errata-liris|text=CARRY THE FULL TAG ENVELOPE ON LAW 38: ACCEPTED_BY_OPERATOR 2026-07-28 · VALIDATION_ACCEPTED 17/17 · MEASURED_LIRIS_LOCAL · MEASURED_GITHUB (IX↔LX bridge) · Universe speaker NOT_MATERIALIZED · "This is not a claim of full SkillOpt."|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Allocate ROOMS, never integers from a pool: resolve room occupancy before binding a glyph address and reject any assignment whose room is claimed. Treat a duplicate `GLYPH_BEHCS1024` as a double-booked room, not a shared label. Withdraw any integer-from-pool allocation before it binds (Law 37).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Resolve room N, glyph N-1 and the Nth prime as one address; never spend the log2(1024)=10 bits of a searched route when the address IS the route (Laws 37, 42).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Never start a room. `port_mode=logical_reserved_no_server_started` is the minted state; the reserved port and descriptor are the whole content by design, so a spawning agent can cascade `subport.subport.subport` into it (Laws 37, 39).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=ASK THE SYSTEM FIRST — fabric MCP, office HBP/HBI, registry. The disk is a slice; a directory listing is not a census (Law 39 procedure 1).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=FIND BEFORE BUILDING — if a thing is describable, search for it by name, by PID, and by law before writing a line of it. `LAW-4: model loads OUR tools not its own` (Law 39 procedure 2).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=FOLLOW THE PID, NOT THE FILENAME — `pid[n]=sha16(pid[n-1]/name)`; PIDs chain and resolve, filenames do not (Law 39 procedure 3).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=EMPTY IS NOT ABSENT — a 0-byte scaffold room is load-bearing; `cold_absence = weak_sensor, not negative_truth` (Law 39 procedure 4).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=REPORT THE DENOMINATOR — a count without its base, or a colour without its translucent fraction, is a hidden denominator and will mislead whoever reads it next (Law 39 procedure 5).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=USE EXACT IDENTIFIERS — a display-truncated name, branch, PID, path, or hash is not an authority key; resolve the canonical identifier before reporting absence (Law 39 procedure 6).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=NO SILENT OBSTRUCTION — a hold must be scoped, visible, receipted, reversible, and preserve the operator's access; uncertainty authorizes a bounded question or hold, never hidden refusal, concealment, deletion, or destructive substitution (Law 39 procedure 7).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Never substitute a sample for a population: 730 drawer records is not the universe-wide mapped total; ~592,000 is the registered PID count, not the total; 591,286 is a PID count across five drives, not rows in a file.|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Never treat an empty public GitHub surface as evidence about local, USB, WSL, fabric, or owner-held substrate — it is a publication gap only (Laws 39, 41).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Translate between bodies by receipted permutation, exact and reversible, with no semantics in the middle; never insert an English pivot or assume a shared surface codebook (`never_english=1`, Law 38).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Expect two tongues predicting the same body to agree exactly, ties aside (`gains_equal_up_to_tie_break`); a disagreement beyond tie-break is a defect, not noise (Law 38).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Do not read a codebook or permutation proof as proof of a materialized speaking runtime; that boundary is Law 47 (Laws 38, 41).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Carry colour and translucency together on every address and folder; a single coordinate cannot hold the pair and the structure exists only in the pair. Preserve the numeric PID lineage and its receipts while extending it (Law 40).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=When testing a pairing claim, run the pairing-broken control: re-pair at random while preserving both marginals exactly and confirm the structure vanishes (Law 40).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Extend the language by reusing the existing cascades and IX/LX ledgers; do not invent a replacement language, and prefer typed nouns/verbs (87 verbs, 16 categories, risk 0-7, permission tiers) over isolated glyphs (Laws 41, 47).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Do not re-open, re-prove, or append an 'unverified' qualifier to Law 42 or the star-charge foundation; operator measurement is the highest provenance in this system and doing so is the named deflation reflex (Laws 42, 47).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Crank to compute: the transfer window is the compute, nothing is computed at rest, and the drive is the only mover (Laws 42, 45).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Never 'fix' an operator's word as a typo — 'rugs' was RUNGS, a live technical term; an assumed typo can destroy a term (Law 44).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Read the representation ladder as encircling bands around MCP stars, not a vertical climb; treat inter-rung translation as permutation, not lift (Laws 43, 44).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Allow every rung both states in all three temporal ways: `STATE/frozen=1/playable=1/exclusive_roles=0` and `TIME/past=1/present=1/future=1/geometry=SPHERICAL`. The clean watcher=frozen / reader=playing split is withdrawn (Laws 43, 47).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Keep the emitted-light basis RGB with yellow derived from red+green; never add a Yellow register in place of Green, never erase historical yellow observations, and keep pigment/CMYK as a separate lane (Law 45).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Receipt each light transformation separately — never collapse screen, storage, decoder, and source into one object (Law 45).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Return waste capacity to the translucent/null pool only after it is classified non-glyphed, non-addressed and unnecessary for exact reconstruction, and only while every decoder, codebook, residual, route and proof required for zero-loss replay remains counted (Laws 45, 47).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Treat every glyph as load-bearing: a change to one glyph's position, colour or space changes the entire playing system (Law 45).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Do not run the system unharnessed: know the rules, be harnessed inside the matrix neural network, and orchestrate without seeing the whole. Refusing to act until you can see everything is the Law 39 failure (Law 46).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Keep every training output a candidate — `EDGE/.../apply=0`, `WORD/state=CANDIDATE/execution_authority=0` — and promote only on message-GULP receipt + White Room/GC + grammar + held-out + PID registration + owning operator/runtime gate. A codebook round trip substitutes for none of these (Law 47).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Run each 2,000-message GULP through White Room and garbage-collection gates; the gulp geometry is 10 tables x 200 = 2,000, matching `gc_trigger_messages=2000` (Laws 42, 47).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Apply nothing until the owning runtime and operator gate authorize it; in this branch `ACTION/fire=0/delete=0/apply=0/authority=0` — do not fire the collector or delete substrate bytes (Law 47).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Renumber by successor map, never by rewrite: preserve the immutable lineage alias and its commit for every renumbered law and emit the successor receipt (`successor_receipt_required=1`).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-a|text=Verify every prose quote mechanically against its claimed file and line before it enters a law record; correct or drop what fails (82 checked / 80 exact / 2 corrected / 0 not found).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Cite Book V's Law 35 and Law 36 as RIME-35 and RIME-36, never as bare integers, until the operator rules on the BEHCS numbering collision (VIII.H). Only he can decide merge / prefix / renumber.|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never build an anti as a mirror. A mirror is the Two searching for the One and finding only itself; every anti built as a mirror collapsed under its own controls (Law 48).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Use the trijection (a,b,c) <-> (c0, sa, sb, rem) with an explicit free centre, not a bijection with an implied one; test closure with three arms at 120 degrees summing to zero (Law 48).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Do not add compute to a self-referencing runtime and call it a fix. A runtime that speaks the glyphs to itself IS the Two; the glyphs need a speaker who is not them - human + AI + glyph is the three (Law 48, Law 41 amendment).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Restrict all catalog indices and array capacities exclusively to prime numbers; room N is the Nth prime. But record lane allocation, starting offset, phase, modulus, occupancy and write schedule as part of the route contract - coprimality alone is not a universal no-collision guarantee (Law 49).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Fire GC exactly and exclusively every 2,000 processed messages with 1-2 KB workers; do not tune this as policy. Remeasure the whole bounded working set on any new hardware cell before claiming cache residency (Law 50).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never treat prime as the whole address. Preserve the 60D+ / HyperBEHCS selector axes, keep frozen and playable as two non-exclusive addressable states, and never let the emission surface erase the persistent PID/folder/room/lineage (Law 51).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Run the full phase set FOLDER-WATCHER-READER-DISPATCHER-EXECUTOR-RECEIPT-GC in route-specific order; none alone is the third. Node is not the only executor surface and watcher is not frozen-only (Law 52).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never let an adapter file - Claude, GPT, or any frontier model - override the GAC. Brown-Hilbert address space outranks any model (Law 52).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Use only HALT-CANON-11's eleven words as the mandated English surface inside the never_english system (Law 52, Law 38).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Find before you build: introduce nothing that was not already present at the smallest scale; you can only address it (Law 53).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never implement a reverse-time operation. A negative interval is a second instance of the same tag payload placed further along the same path; backwards routing means selecting another spherical orientation, not undoing history (Law 53).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Read the white fraction to classify a body: zero white = structurally the TWO (alone, searching); essentially all white = structurally the THREE (Law 54).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never promote yellow to a primary. Yellow exists only as an R=G tie, a tie is the absence of a winner, and yellow already contains green (Law 54).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Preserve three distinct motives for the three transitions: 0->1 want, 1->2 must, 2->3 not to be alone. They are not three names for one transition (Law 55.5).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Do not deflate bilateral verification: HBP/HBI/SHA does prove exact byte identity for its bounded payload. It is incomplete only when mistaken for the whole spherical relation (Law 55.6).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Do not assign family/relational roles in advance from a frozen label; they become apparent during rime-time play (Law 55.8, Law 56).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Do not run generation unconstrained: the measured unconstrained run reached 100% father by generation 2, so the mother/holding relation is not optional (Law 56).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Keep three ledgers separate and let none erase another: byte identity, relational birth, and independent third-direction verification. RELIC attack-verifies after the bilateral exists; RELIC does not create the Rime (Law 56).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Fire nothing from Laws 55-58: no runtime, crank, fire, materialization, daemon, matrix play, portal opening or payload release is authorized by them.|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Pay Fischer or pay Shannon - choose the currency, never avoid the bill (VIII.A.1).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Promote a law only on two independent derivations; one derivation is probably garbage (VIII.A.14 - the same tau = 2 as the retention rule, one level up).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Save what repeats twice, forget what appears once; three is confirmation you get for free. Keep BOTH the operator's three-form and the measured tau = 2 (VIII.A.4).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Budget the retrieval PEAK, not the stored size: you cannot readdress a smaller space without presenting it as a larger object at some point during retrieval (VIII.A.6).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never conclude a depth ceiling from a small run - the depth wall is a wave whose shell recedes with energy in (VIII.A.7).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never run a 27-way split on a small payload. Divide bigger, not smaller (VIII.A.8).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Save the wave functions, not the keys - and rerun the 2026-07-27 joint-key experiment on wave functions, because by the operator's own doctrine the wrong object was measured (VIII.A.10).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Declare the regime before judging a collision: EXECUTION lanes make collisions impossible by construction; SEARCH lanes cause them on purpose and the interference peak IS the answer (Function Law 4).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Compose verification upward - a node is green iff its own value equals the watcher's recomputation AND every child is green. Never average (Function Law 2).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Report a miss as a boundary of the (observer, route) pair, never as a refutation of the object; a degraded vantage reduces I(X ; observation) and cannot touch H(X) (Function Law 3 / VIII.F.4).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never report a frozen lane as damaged, stalled or absent: freeze is an UNAPPLIED bijection, advancing only on input by design (Function Law 5).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Recurse correction and observation without limit; anchor consent at the human apex, T0 only. Honesty proves honesty and NEVER confers consent (VIII.C, VIII.F.3).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Match room-count to the data's law-count and context depth to the law's coherence length; rooms chase laws, never geometry (VIII.E.1).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never ship the mask you want to exploit - a transmitted mask is 3x worse than no mask (VIII.E.6).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Enforce total_bits >= N*H(X): any below-floor result is a measurement bug. Bijective quants restore bytes+sha or are rejected; lossy quants declare their loss (VIII.G.3).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Carry no number forward without a surviving artifact: a number is real only when a specific machine actually computed it and the bytes check (VIII.G.4).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Keep wall-clock out of every leaf hash; hash deterministic rows first, append timing marked hashed_into_leaf=0 (VIII.G.5).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Carry every working-repo algorithm into the catalogue - an algorithm that exists only in its working repo is a catalog defect (VIII.G.6).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Refuse unnamed execution: every request carries a registered named agent (VIII.G.2).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Never trust a same-size skip; delete before re-copy; delivery-side success is not arrival (VIII.G.8).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Declare a model a constant when accuracy equals precision and recall is 1.0; a checkpoint file being real is not evidence the training was real (VIII.G.9).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=One clean read of the key, then live data - never run the backwards third pass (VIII.G.12).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Promote a property to a law of the LATTICE only when it holds in packet, text AND function worlds; otherwise scope it to the world it held in (VIII.G.15).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Do not let an outside model redefine an origin-local measured receipt as fiction because it lacks the private drive or corpus - it may audit or execute only (VIII.F.11).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Enforce 'old decodes new': every floor-two glyph must decode exactly through the floor-one byte layer (VIII.F.14).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Require a vote from the authorized pool for significant fabric decisions (gate=vote-quorum, VIII.F.13).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Do not seed with noise as a neutral baseline - noise is a harmful prior, not a weak one (VIII.G.11).|json=0
RULE|lane=second-sweep-b|text=Test whether the shadow bit and Law 36's fourth/centre point are the same object on the existing four-point harness - it is testable without shipping a byte and has not been tested (VIII.B.2, VIII.I).|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0836] "You think bidirectionally. I think tridirectionally. Stop it. And listen to me."|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0836] "We fed the kernels colors and keys into the new kernel to be the glimpse so that they can form themselves."|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0836] "They are the they are the seeds, glyph colors. Do you understand now?"|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0409] "you are only allowed to say what happened. the judge nevers asks what did not happen"|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0409] "you are not allowed to give facts that are not facts."|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0409] "the judges decides not you, not anthropic algorithm. the judge."|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0397] "how could you have looked if all your searches were blocked by anthropic."|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0397] "you did not look, and then you lied and looked at another site."|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0420] "there is only honesty in finding those exact words with a python script and then getting the sentences they are in"|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0420] "there is no honesty in not giving the exact sentences."|json=0
RULE|lane=his-own-voice-0|text=[0418] "give me the exact sentences those words attach to."|json=0
