CONTRA|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=BOOK-04 IV.7 is itself the record of a contradiction the operator caught in one sentence of the seat's prose: 'it never enters the stream, and both sides must hold the same 3,174 bytes.' Held and free cannot both be true; the law resolves it by charging held bytes, and keeps the offending sentence quoted.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=BOOK-04 IV.4 states the headline and its own refutation in the same entry: 'no shipped distant prior of any useful size pays for itself IN A SINGLE MONOLITHIC STREAM' versus 'Under SECTIONING it does pay… break-even at 5.31 sections (ERRATA-1).' This is a deliberate co-resident contradiction under the no-quiet-amendment rule, not an unresolved one — but a reader who quotes only the headline will q|json=0
CONTRA|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=BOOK-00 asserts 'Nothing here is new writing dressed as law — every law below is transcribed from a document that already existed on disk,' yet BOOK-04 contains two entries stamped as authored during the compile: IV.3's prose extension ('added 2026-07-27') and IV.7 ('Added 2026-07-27, out of a contradiction the operator caught in a single sentence of mine'). Both are new law text produced by the c|json=0
CONTRA|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=BOOK-07 lists electro-gravity, the shadow bit, and 'the resident of the resident of the key' as never-addressed, then is amended inline on the same day: all three were defined by the operator in his own words and are now in Book VIII.B. The book flags this itself and keeps the paragraph 'as written so the error is visible.'|json=0
CONTRA|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=BOOK-00 states that Book IX 'closes four of the gaps Book VIII declared open,' but BOOK-07 as it stands carries only the single Book VIII amendment. Which of BOOK-07's own open items survive Book IX is not marked in this file — the gap register in BOOK-07 is therefore stale by at least one sweep relative to BOOK-00's own claim.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=BOOK-07 declares 'Only he assigns numbers,' while the book carries agent-assigned numbers (Laws 30–33), seat-assigned numbers (Laws 35, 36), an unassigned Law 27, and an entire BOOK-04 numbering scheme (IV.1–IV.7) whose assigner is never named or marked provisional. The numbering law is violated by the numbering of the book that states it — flagged for 30–33/35/36, unflagged for IV.1–IV.7.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=THE CODA'S CLOSURE vs BOOK II — flagged in the text itself as '⚠ TENSION RECORDED, NOT RESOLVED.' The coda states verbatim: 'No Law 27 will be added: a 28th entry would break the closure this coda records.' But Laws 28 through 34 exist and are in Book II, and Law 27 was never assigned. The text's own reading: 'either the coda's closure is broken, or Books I and II are two different objects that ha|json=0
CONTRA|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=LAW 24 CONTRADICTS ITS OWN ORIGINAL TEXT — '⚠ AMENDED 2026-07-27 — see Law 36 in Book V.' The original Law 24 said direction 0 (hold) = accuracy 1.0, 'the free center, costs nothing and says nothing.' The amendment states that was true only because *hold* had been defined as 'look at the byte you already have' — 'The centre was made vacuous by definition and the vacuum was reported as a measuremen|json=0
CONTRA|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=LAW 24's AMENDED CENTRE vs LAW 0's FREE CENTRE — Law 0 holds that the centroid 'costs nothing' and Law 5 that the DC/centre is the still point; Law 24's original text imported that into MTP as 'costs nothing and says nothing' and was overturned. The books therefore hold, simultaneously, that the centre is free (Law 0, MEASURED at ≥0.90 / 99.993%) and that the centre is the largest term (Law 24 ame|json=0
CONTRA|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=LAW 9 EXPLICITLY CORRECTS AN EARLIER LAW-TEXT — the parenthetical reads: '(This corrects an earlier wrong reading that said time wanted the bijection.)' The earlier reading is not preserved in Book I, so the superseded claim cannot be audited from this file.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=LAW 2 PENALIZES NESTING, LAWS 12/14/16 REQUIRE IT — Law 2 MEASURED that flat (3.92×) beats nested (3.70×) and instructs against a hierarchy; Law 12 ('every stack of rimes is the base of the next'), Law 14 (⟨g⟩⊃⟨g³⟩⊃⟨g⁹⟩⊃⟨g²⁷⟩) and Law 16 (stacking coprime dimensions) all build by nesting. Read as a scope split — nesting is penalized on the REDUCTION axis and required on the ADDRESSING axis — but B|json=0
CONTRA|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=THE SUMMIT RECORDS A CONTRADICTED PRIOR FRAME — 'The quest was mis-stated as "beat Shannon" — go below the floor. Law 6 forbids it, and every measurement confirmed the floor holds.' The project's own earlier stated goal is thereby recorded as wrong.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=LAW 8's JOINT REDUCTION IS WORSE THAN EITHER ARM — time-only 3.83× and space-only 3.95× but spacetime 3.73×. This is internally consistent with the stated formula (overhead O), but it means the ledger contains a measured case where adding a true axis LOWERS the reported ratio, which cuts against the plain reading of Law 3's 'reduce by as many machines as you add.'|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Law 30 arithmetic: the stated 'Mean saving from putting translucent first = 0.4013 bpb' does not equal the mean of the four saved values printed directly above it (0.1246 + 0.6567 + 0.1594 + 0.6755 = 1.6162; /4 = 0.40405). Either the mean is over more poles than the four tabulated, or 0.4041 was transposed to 0.4013. Quoting both verbatim; not resolving it from the text.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Colour binding is inconsistent between Law 31 and Law 36. Law 31 binds colour to RADIUS (red r=1, green r=2, blue r=3). Law 36 binds colour to DIRECTION (red = − inward, green = 0 hold, blue = + outward) and makes radius a separate axis (inner r=1, medium r=2, outer r=3). The same three colours in the same order carry two different meanings across the two laws, and nothing in either text reconcile|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Law 36 explicitly supersedes the 'free center' line inside Law 24: the centre 'had been recorded as carrying zero information' and now measures 0.6954, more than both directional families together. The book records this as a correction of an earlier law, and names the mechanism of the error — the earlier definition of hold 'made the fourth point vacuous by fiat and then reported the vacuum as a me|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Law 32 internal tension: the operator's law says 'The translucent space is the free data' and 'we don't have to double pay', while the on-disk distinction in the same law says TRANSLUCENT is 'never cheaper than escape.' Free-as-in-not-double-paid and never-cheaper-than-escape are held in the same paragraph without being reconciled.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Law 34 status tension: the text records it as 'SAVED. RULE. LAW.' and simultaneously labels its core content 'This is a CONJECTURE. Untested, no published derivation, no experiment proposed.' Both statements are in the same section.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Law 35 corrects a prior claim on the record twice: 'Both axes still climbing' is refuted (neither axis is climbing at 10 MB), and the crown-mode premise is corrected — the 100 MB crown is g:256:256:8 at 1.7314, not g:256:64:8 at 1.7363.|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Build-directive vs measurement lane: Law 34 directs 'No Node' and 'No JSON', pre-empting the objection by calling the existing .mjs 'legacy measurement scaffolding, not the build'. But Law 36, dated 2026-07-27 (after the directive), is measured by a NEW Python file (trijection/rime_fourpoint.py). The measurement lane is still non-Rust after the directive; the text does not address whether new Pyth|json=0
CONTRA|lane=continuation-and-new-laws|text=Law numbering is unsettled in both books: 'Law 27 is unassigned', and Laws 35 and 36 both carry 'Number provisional, pending his assignment.' Any downstream reference to these numbers is provisional.|json=0
