CONTRA|lane=his-own-voice-4|text=THE CORPUS NAME IS UNSTABLE ACROSS TURNS. He corrects it once — "asolaria , not anilliary" (turn 0715) — but the transcript then carries ancillary (0748, 0774), axillary (0724, 0784), maxillary (0762), acid area (0751), SLAria (0724), acidaria (0823), aceleria (0804), asularia (0752, 0825). These are ASR variants of one name, but the book preserves them unmarked, so a machine reading the rules lit|json=0
CONTRA|lane=his-own-voice-4|text=BIT ACCOUNTING IS INCONSISTENT ACROSS TURNS. Turn 0708: "two bits that is red, and one bit is translucent". Turn 0734: "The keys are the two bit version of the wave functions three bit cell". Turn 0751 gives a five-symbol table 0-4. Turn 0799: "6 bits per 1". Turn 0685-0686: one bit red, two bits green, loss at blue. No single accounting reconciles these.|json=0
