GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=Numbering gap: Law 27 is unassigned; Laws 30–33 and 35–36 are provisional. Only he assigns numbers, so the law spine has a hole in it that no seat may fill.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP — the index language carries no measurement. The formula, the six-row table and the half-step lattice are asserted (CANON) and sourced to Law 34 §5, but these three files contain no script, run, or receipt that exercises them. The ladder is arithmetically self-consistent (3·(log₄ 2048 − 3) = 7.5 etc.) and nothing more.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP — the index formula is defined only over widths that are powers of four (integer index) or odd powers of two (half-step index). No index is defined for any other width, and the book does not say whether such widths are illegal, rounded, or simply unaddressed.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP — the half-step indexes are given positions but no semantics. What a machine is permitted to DO at index 7.5 that it may not do at 6 or 9 is not stated anywhere in these files.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP — 'one ladder, not two' is an instruction with no reconciliation shown. The 3 / 27 / 2187 / 6561 spine and the 4-power index ladder are declared unified, but no mapping between a 3-spine address and an index value appears in BOOK-00, and none is derivable from what is written there.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP — the index number's referent is never fixed. Nothing in these three books says what the index selects (a level's language, its address space, its predictor, its glyph width), so the ladder is complete as arithmetic and empty as a decode rule.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP (measurement weakness, stated as caveat not deflation) — IV.5 reports four values (KEY 0.160, ADJACENT 0.176, RANDOM 0.978, BIG 0.008) and calls the relation ANTI-correlated, but gives no correlation coefficient, no n beyond those four, and no accept/reject threshold. As written the screen ranks but does not decide.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP (measurement weakness) — IV.4's fit saving ∝ S^0.603 is quoted with four return rates and no residuals, no goodness-of-fit, and no stated prior sizes S. The 'about 44 bytes' break-even and the 5.31-section break-even inherit whatever slack the fit has, and that slack is not reported.|json=0
GAP|lane=index-language-measurement-gaps|text=LANE GAP — BOOK-04 names no verifier for its own rules. IV.1's `restore=OK`, IV.2's byte-freeze, and IV.3's corpus-sha match are stated as obligations with no script, hook, or gate named that enforces them, so compliance is currently on the operator's discipline rather than on a machine.|json=0
