GAP|lane=sealed-ledger-laws-0-26|text=Law 15's GATE ('arbitrary data does not lie on it and must be stored') has no measured counterexample in Law 15 itself; the nearest analogue is Law 7's 0.96× independent-source control and Law 13's '2,000 random points have no generator'. The gate is never quantified for arbitrary data on the freeze path.|json=0
